.IX Title "EVP_SIGNATURE-SM2 7ossl"
.TH EVP_SIGNATURE-SM2 7ossl 2026-04-14 4.0.0 OpenSSL
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
EVP_SIGNATURE\-SM2 \- The EVP_PKEY SM2 signature implementation.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Support for computing SM2 signatures.
See \fBEVP_PKEY\-SM2\fR\|(7) for information related to SM2 keys.
.PP
This signature algorithm can be explicitly fetched with
\&\fBEVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex2\fR\|(3), and implicitly fetched (through SM2
keys) with \fBEVP_DigestSignInit_ex\fR\|(3) and
\&\fBEVP_DigestVerifyInit_ex\fR\|(3).
.SS "SM2 Signature Parameters"
.IX Subsection "SM2 Signature Parameters"
The following signature parameters can be set using
\&\fBEVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params\fR\|(3), \fBEVP_DigestSignInit_ex\fR\|(3) or
\&\fBEVP_DigestVerifyInit_ex\fR\|(3).
.IP """digest"" (\fBOSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST\fR) <UTF8 string>" 4
.IX Item """digest"" (OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST) <UTF8 string>"
This defaults to the \f(CW\*(C`SM3\*(C'\fR digest if not explicitly specified.
.IP """digest-size"" (\fBOSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST\fR) <size_t>" 4
.IX Item """digest-size"" (OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST) <size_t>"
This defaults to 32 bytes if not explicitly specified.
Digests of a different size are not supported with \fBSM2\fR.
.IP """distid"" (\fBOSSL_PKEY_PARAM_DIST_ID\fR) <UTF8 string>" 4
.IX Item """distid"" (OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_DIST_ID) <UTF8 string>"
The \fIdistinguishing identifier\fR defaults to \f(CW1234567812345678\fR if not
explicitly specified.
.Sp
An explicit empty distinguishing identifier value may need to be used to verify
or create signatures that are compatible with versions of OpenSSL prior to 4.0.
With the commandline tools an empty value can be specified with the use of
either the \fB\-pkeyopt\fR (\fBopenssl\-pkeyutl\fR\|(1)) or \fB\-sigopt\fR
(\fBopenssl\-dgst\fR\|(1)) option with a value of \f(CW\*(C`distid:\*(C'\fR.
.IP """tls-version"" (\fBOSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_TLS_VERSION\fR) <uint>" 4
.IX Item """tls-version"" (OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_TLS_VERSION) <uint>"
The OpenSSL 4.0 or later TLS protocol engine passes this parameter to the
underlying signature algorithm when signing or verifying TLS
\&\fBCertificateVerify\fR messages.
When the protocol version is TLS 1.3 (0x0304), the SM2 signature algorithm will
use the RFC8998 \fIdistinguished identifier\fR instead of the default value noted
above.
.PP
The following signature parameters can be retrieved using
\&\fBEVP_PKEY_CTX_get_params()\fR.
.IP """algorithm-id"" (\fBOSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_ALGORITHM_ID\fR) <octet string>" 4
.IX Item """algorithm-id"" (OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_ALGORITHM_ID) <octet string>"
This returns the DER encoding of the \fBSM2\-with\-SM3\fR signature OID.
.IP """digest"" (\fBOSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST\fR) <UTF8 string>" 4
.IX Item """digest"" (OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST) <UTF8 string>"
.PD 0
.IP """digest-size"" (\fBOSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST\fR) <size_t>" 4
.IX Item """digest-size"" (OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST) <size_t>"
.PD
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBEVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params\fR\|(3),
\&\fBEVP_PKEY_sign\fR\|(3),
\&\fBEVP_PKEY_verify\fR\|(3),
\&\fBEVP_DigestSignInit_ex\fR\|(3),
\&\fBEVP_DigestVerifyInit_ex\fR\|(3),
\&\fBprovider\-signature\fR\|(7),
.SH HISTORY
.IX Header "HISTORY"
The default value of the SM2 distinguishing identifier changed from empty to
\&\f(CW1234567812345678\fR as of OpenSSL 4.0.
.PP
Support for the \fBOSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_TLS_VERSION\fR parameter was added in
OpenSSL 4.0.
